    "title": "8 Anaheim High School running team members struck by suspected DUI driver, police say - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Abigail Velez ,\n5 hours ago\nEight students on the Anaheim High School running team were injured after a suspected DUI driver plowed into them Wednesday afternoon, police said.\nThe high school students were waiting at the intersection of Harbor Boulevard and W. North Street when they were hit by a car that went off the road just before 3 p.m., according to the Anaheim Police Department.\nPolice said eight students, between 16 and 17 years old, were struck. Three were immediately taken to a hospital.\nEight members of the Anaheim High School running team were hurt when a vehicle plowed into them at a street intersection, police said.\nEyewitness News obtained surveillance video from a nearby business that shows a red Toyota veer right and barrel toward the corner where the students were standing.\nA 27-year-old driver was also taken to a hospital in unknown condition. He was later arrested on suspicion of DUI.\nAt least eight members of the Anaheim High School running team were hurt when a vehicle plowed into them at a street intersection, police said.\nPolice said a coach was running with the students and was coming up to the intersection when he witnessed the crash. Another coach told Eyewitness News that one of the injured runners was in critical condition.\nSchool resource officers were on scene following the incident.\n5",
